    """Code a function to clamp a given number between a minimum value and maximum value. However, if the given number is negative, return the absolute value of the number before clamping it. The input number can be a floating-point number and the minimum and maximum values can be floating-point numbers as well. Additionally, if the input number is within a certain range, return a string indicating its proximity to the range boundary. The range is defined as being within 10% of the minimum or maximum value. 

